    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d603">

                <pb facs="0636" n="524" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg524"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-05-07"><hi rendition="#italic">May 7,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 74.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am profoundly grieved to inform you that
                    I have received a cable message from Sir Edward Grey announcing the demise of
                    the King last evening at 11.45.</p>
                <p>It is my melancholy duty to request that you will bring the sad intelligence to
                    the knowledge of the President and his Cabinet.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James Bryce.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
